[
    {
        "id": "nguyen-thanh-2020",
        "artistId": "nguyen-thanh",
        "year": "2020",
        "title": "In Full Bloom",
        "slug": "2020",
        "theme": "\"IN FULL BLOOM\"",
        "description": "<p>With a rich diversity of themes and an unrelenting dedication over his 25-year artistic journey, <strong>Nguyen Thanh<\/strong> has continuously explored, learned, and reinvented himself, creating ever-new, distinctive bodies of work that captivate viewers and lead them from one emotional state to another.<\/p><p>Through these concerns and contemplations, the artist persistently sends out messages of tranquility — stories of a green world and a vision of peace for humankind.<\/p>",
        "featuredImage": "..\/..\/images\/artists\/Nguyen Thanh\/2020\/2020_1.jpg",
        "artworkCount": 6,
        "published": true,
        "displayOrder": 1
    },
    {
        "id": "nguyen-thanh-2019",
        "artistId": "nguyen-thanh",
        "year": "2019",
        "title": "Blooming Radiance",
        "slug": "2019",
        "theme": "\"BLOOMING RADIANCE\"",
        "description": "<p>Like a clear reminder and an explicit message, <strong>Nguyen Thanh<\/strong> addresses the world with a simple yet urgent call: \"Let us join hands to protect the Earth, to preserve a green planet for today and for generations to come.\" This statement extends and deepens the spirit of his earlier theme \"Green Planet,\" reinforcing his consistent concern for the environment and human destiny.<\/p>\n                            <p>In \"Connection\", that message becomes more resolute, almost like a prayer or a plea charged with empathy. The artist depicts lines, paths, and cords intertwined and bound together with tight knots — visual metaphors for unity and solidarity. As he explains: \"Let us stay united — all of us. Unity is strength, the enduring bond that carries us toward the shores of peace and happiness.\"<\/p>\n                            <p>Rendered in an abstract language, these works embody his decisive use of color and form, conveying both urgency and hope. Through this theme, <strong>Nguyen Thanh<\/strong> entrusts his aspirations to the canvas — a vision of a future world that is green, harmonious, and grounded in human connection.<\/p>",
        "featuredImage": "..\/..\/images\/artists\/Nguyen Thanh\/2019\/2019_1.jpg",
        "artworkCount": 6,
        "published": true,
        "displayOrder": 2
    },
    {
        "id": "nguyen-thanh-2016",
        "artistId": "nguyen-thanh",
        "year": "2016",
        "title": "Green Planet",
        "slug": "2016",
        "theme": "\"GREEN PLANET\"",
        "description": "<p>With tireless creativity and dedication, <strong>Nguyen Thanh<\/strong> continually explores new narratives and emotions, renewing both his brushwork and color language across diverse themes, each one a story he shares with art lovers at home and abroad.<\/p>\n                            <p>From earlier compositions that evoked a sense of peace, he moves into a strikingly different visual realm of tension and contrast, as if multiple emotional currents within him are waiting for the moment of release. Human figures appear to be flying around a great sphere, sometimes soaring upward, sometimes spiraling inward, with trees and natural forms drawn into the same orbit — suggesting a profound inner concern.<\/p>\n                            <p>As the artist reflects: \"Nature has given us precious and beautiful things; if humanity does not know how to use and preserve them, they may shatter. Let us protect our green planet — not only for today, but for tomorrow.\" The recurring image of spherical forms floating in space alludes to galaxies in constant motion, reminding viewers of a living, fragile universe that demands awareness and responsibility.<\/p>",
        "featuredImage": "..\/..\/images\/artists\/Nguyen Thanh\/2016\/z7571028455031_39e0cdf8ef03e22528c5adeadc181649.jpg",
        "artworkCount": 6,
        "published": true,
        "displayOrder": 3
    },
    {
        "id": "nguyen-thanh-2010",
        "artistId": "nguyen-thanh",
        "year": "2010",
        "title": "A Peaceful Space Above the City",
        "slug": "2010",
        "theme": "\"A PEACEFUL SPACE ABOVE THE CITY\"",
        "description": "<p>Following a period of intense emotion and powerful, decisive brushwork that led viewers into the radiant light of the cosmos, <strong>Nguyen Thanh<\/strong>'s art reached a striking point of contrast — where vigorous, dynamic strokes met thick, textured layers of paint, rippling like waves across the surface. In this fusion of energy and stillness, the artist seems to have found the light of truth — the light of serenity, a spiritual haven where all beings yearn to dwell.<\/p>\n                            <p>Through his paintings, <strong>Nguyen Thanh<\/strong> evokes a tranquil, poetic atmosphere, marked by deliberate spaces of emptiness — peaceful and contemplative. His palette softens into gentle hues of pale orange, warm gray, and quiet amber tones that radiate an almost meditative calm.<\/p>\n                            <p>As the artist reflects: \"The silence within is not rest, nor cessation — it is a stillness that regenerates, where inner stories are quietly in motion, transforming endlessly toward subtle prosperity.\"<\/p>\n                            <p>This theme became one of <strong>Nguyen Thanh<\/strong>'s most distinguished artistic phases, earning him the Grand Excellence Award in Miami, Florida, USA, in December 2025. With participation from over twenty countries and more than three thousand artists worldwide, the recognition affirmed his dedication, persistence, and ever-evolving creative journey.<\/p>",
        "featuredImage": "..\/..\/images\/artists\/Nguyen Thanh\/2010\/mebeo.png",
        "artworkCount": 3,
        "published": true,
        "displayOrder": 4
    },
    {
        "id": "nguyen-thanh-2008",
        "artistId": "nguyen-thanh",
        "year": "2008",
        "title": "The Light of Heaven and Earth",
        "slug": "2008",
        "theme": "\"THE LIGHT OF HEAVEN AND EARTH\"",
        "description": "<p>Continuing his exploration of everyday life — from the quiet rhythm of rural landscapes to the dynamic pulse of urban scenes — <strong>Nguyen Thanh<\/strong>'s work during this period reflects a deep and evolving meditation on human existence and nature's harmony. Through different phases and across time, he constructs his visual narratives with layered pigments and textured brushstrokes, translating simple daily moments into poetic reflections on life.<\/p>\n                            <p>\"The Light : Heaven & Earth,\" <strong>Nguyen Thanh<\/strong>'s 2008 theme, stands as a luminous continuation of this creative journey. At its core lies his fascination with light — expressed through vigorous brush movements and overlapping layers of green, red, and yellow that merge into powerful, symbolic compositions. These bold and contemporary strokes open a vast pictorial space — the light of the sky, the light of the earth — as a metaphor for the divine energy uniting all beings.<\/p>\n                            <p>As the artist reflects: \"The light of heaven and earth — the light gifted by nature to all living things, to our planet — is something we must cherish and protect, never let it fade.\"<\/p>\n                            <p>The interplay of vibrant yellows, resolute reds, and luminous greens infuses his canvases with an emotional resonance that guides the viewer toward the radiant beauty of the universe — a space where earthly and celestial light meet in harmony.<\/p>",
        "featuredImage": "..\/..\/images\/artists\/Nguyen Thanh\/2008\/nguoi1.png",
        "artworkCount": 4,
        "published": true,
        "displayOrder": 5
    },
    {
        "id": "nguyen-thanh-2007",
        "artistId": "nguyen-thanh",
        "year": "2007",
        "title": "Memories at Seventeen",
        "slug": "2007",
        "theme": "\"MEMORIES AT SEVENTEEN\"",
        "description": "<p>Each theme in <strong>Nguyen Thanh<\/strong>'s body of work unfolds as a story — a continuous emotional stream that reflects his inner world and the passage of time. \"Memories of School Days\" draws inspiration from the recollections of youth — those tender years of innocence and discovery that live within every human being. For <strong>Nguyen Thanh<\/strong>, this was the age of pure light, of school days filled with laughter, sunlight, and rain.<\/p>\n                            <p>The artist revisits these memories through the graceful imagery of white school uniforms fluttering in the wind — under soft morning light or shimmering rain. Layers of white, gray, and brown tones blend delicately with hints of yellow, forming silhouettes that seem to drift effortlessly across the canvas like fleeting moments of youth.<\/p>\n                            <p>Through these works, <strong>Nguyen Thanh<\/strong> captures the essence of innocence and emotional vitality — the spirit of young students, the gentle rhythm of school life, and the radiant light opening beyond the distant horizon. His paintings from this period evoke not only nostalgia but also a quiet optimism — the enduring brightness of memory and hope.<\/p>",
        "featuredImage": "..\/..\/images\/artists\/Nguyen Thanh\/2007\/girl1.png",
        "artworkCount": 5,
        "published": true,
        "displayOrder": 6
    },
    {
        "id": "nguyen-thanh-2006",
        "artistId": "nguyen-thanh",
        "year": "2006",
        "title": "The Colors of Nature",
        "slug": "2006",
        "theme": "\"THE COLORS OF NATURE\"",
        "description": "<p>Continuing the creative thread of 2004, this new phase reveals a striking transformation. After a period of quiet stillness, a different kind of rebirth emerges — a stillness that exists not to end movement, but to restore and recharge the very energy of life.<\/p>\n                            <p>In this series, flowers burst into radiant bloom across all spaces, from the inner city to distant suburbs. Hues of green, red, purple, and yellow seem to dance over wide fields, greeting a new day, a new era filled with promise. The vibrant stir of color suggests a renewed state of mind in the artist — a love for life, a sense of trust, optimism, and joy.<\/p>\n                            <p>As he shares: \"The flowers stretch upright and show their colors despite wind and dew — like the image of the young generation of the future.\" Through these works, the blossoms become symbols of resilience and aspiration, standing tall amid change and shining with their own quiet strength.<\/p>",
        "featuredImage": "..\/..\/images\/artists\/Nguyen Thanh\/2006\/2006_1.jpg",
        "artworkCount": 6,
        "published": true,
        "displayOrder": 7
    },
    {
        "id": "nguyen-thanh-2004",
        "artistId": "nguyen-thanh",
        "year": "2004",
        "title": "Suburb and Stillness",
        "slug": "2004",
        "theme": "\"SUBURB AND STILLNESS\"",
        "description": "<p>The year 2004 marks a distinct turning point in <strong>Nguyen Thanh's<\/strong> artistic expression, shifting toward quieter, more contemplative subjects.<\/p>",
        "featuredImage": "..\/..\/images\/artists\/Nguyen Thanh\/2004\/NT1.png",
